WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.362
Hi, I'm Clementine!

00:00:02.362 --> 00:00:04.862
Ming's design model draws interfaces and posters.

00:00:04.862 --> 00:00:06.291
Its core is borrowed.

00:00:06.291 --> 00:00:09.149
What's new is how a prompt reaches it.

00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:15.210
The idea: keep Z-Image's diffusion transformer, and swap the parts around it.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:20.024
A new encoder, learned query tokens, and a decoder with an alpha channel.

00:00:21.675 --> 00:00:26.189
The prompt goes into a Ming multimodal language model, with two hundred

00:00:26.189 --> 00:00:28.445
and fifty-six learnable query tokens appended.

00:00:28.865 --> 00:00:32.886
Those query states run through a Qwen connector, read both ways, into

00:00:32.886 --> 00:00:35.567
the slot Z-Image's text encoder used to fill.

00:00:35.987 --> 00:00:40.205
In parallel, a shortcut takes layers five, twelve and twenty, and projects

00:00:40.205 --> 00:00:42.314
them straight to the transformer's width.

00:00:42.734 --> 00:00:45.093
The transformer is Z-Image's base checkpoint, fine-tuned.

00:00:45.093 --> 00:00:49.810
It's the six billion in the name, and about a quarter of the download.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:53.483
Its decoder is swapped for Qwen-Image-Layered's RGBA one.

00:00:53.483 --> 00:00:56.736
It fits because both use sixteen latent channels.

00:00:58.583 --> 00:01:02.155
The Layer model reuses the same body, but asks it for frames.

00:01:02.155 --> 00:01:04.238
The first frame is the full composite.

00:01:04.658 --> 00:01:07.321
Then one RGBA layer per frame, front to back.

00:01:07.741 --> 00:01:10.243
The flat input joins as one more frame.

00:01:10.243 --> 00:01:14.623
Read from the code, six layers means eight full frames, run twice per step.

00:01:14.623 --> 00:01:16.812
The layer count is a latency dial.

00:01:18.217 --> 00:01:20.128
What did the fine-tune buy?

00:01:20.128 --> 00:01:23.568
A two-hundred-and-forty-four-point gain over its parent on design prompts.

00:01:23.568 --> 00:01:27.391
First of forty-two open models there, sixteenth of all models.

00:01:28.975 --> 00:01:32.776
So the core is Z-Image's, re-aimed at a new encoder and fine-tuned.

00:01:32.776 --> 00:01:35.310
The arena's gain is what that training bought.

00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:42.256
To recap: a new encoder feeding Z-Image's transformer, an RGBA decoder, and

00:01:42.256 --> 00:01:43.986
layers made as frames.

00:01:44.406 --> 00:01:46.664
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:46.664 --> 00:01:47.309
I'm Clementine.

00:01:47.309 --> 00:01:47.632
Bye!
